## Script 1 — run now (prod3, `harness_comp`)

```
-- CDS-129138 / prod3: restore the plain 5-column unique index on gitops_app_info.
-- The running ng-manager predates timescale migrations 125/127; its
-- ON CONFLICT (accountid, orgidentifier, projectidentifier, agent_id, applicationname)
-- matches no index, so every upsert fails and GitOps licensing undercounts.
-- Aborts without changes if duplicate keys would make the index unbuildable.

BEGIN;

SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '30min';
SET LOCAL lock_timeout      = '30s';

DO $$
DECLARE
  dupe_groups bigint;
BEGIN
  SELECT count(*) INTO dupe_groups
  FROM (
    SELECT 1
    FROM public.gitops_app_info
    WHERE accountid         IS NOT NULL
      AND orgidentifier     IS NOT NULL
      AND projectidentifier IS NOT NULL
      AND agent_id          IS NOT NULL
      AND applicationname   IS NOT NULL
    GROUP BY accountid, orgidentifier, projectidentifier, agent_id, applicationname
    HAVING count(*) > 1
  ) d;

  IF dupe_groups > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION
      'Aborting: % duplicate 5-column key group(s) in gitops_app_info; dedupe required first',
      dupe_groups;
  END IF;

  IF to_regclass('public.gitops_app_info_unique_application_index') IS NOT NULL THEN
    RAISE NOTICE 'gitops_app_info_unique_application_index already exists; nothing to do';
    RETURN;
  END IF;

  EXECUTE 'CREATE UNIQUE INDEX gitops_app_info_unique_application_index '
          'ON public.gitops_app_info USING btree '
          '(accountid, orgidentifier, projectidentifier, agent_id, applicationname)';

  RAISE NOTICE 'Created gitops_app_info_unique_application_index';
END $$;

COMMIT;

-- Verification: expect one row with indisvalid = t, indisunique = t,
-- plus the four gitops_app_info_unique_app_* partial indexes still present.
SELECT c.relname AS index_name, i.indisvalid, i.indisready, i.indisunique
FROM pg_index i
JOIN pg_class c ON c.oid = i.indexrelid
WHERE c.relname LIKE 'gitops_app_info_unique%'
ORDER BY c.relname;
```

Rollback is `DROP INDEX IF EXISTS public.gitops_app_info_unique_application_index;` — which is also script 2.

## Script 2 — run immediately before the new 1.160.xx ng-manager deploy

The new code intentionally writes several rows per app to track service and parent linkage history. This index rejects exactly those inserts, so leaving it in place during the rollout reproduces today's outage in the opposite direction. The guard refuses to drop unless migration 127's four partial indexes are actually present, so you can't end up with no uniqueness at all.

```
-- CDS-129138 / prod3: remove the temporary plain unique index before deploying
-- the ng-manager version that writes multiple gitops_app_info rows per app.
-- Aborts if the four partial unique indexes from migration 127 are not in place.

BEGIN;

SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '30s';

DO $$
DECLARE
  partial_count int;
BEGIN
  SELECT count(*) INTO partial_count
  FROM pg_indexes
  WHERE schemaname = 'public'
    AND tablename  = 'gitops_app_info'
    AND indexname IN (
      'gitops_app_info_unique_app_with_svc_with_parent',
      'gitops_app_info_unique_app_with_svc_without_parent',
      'gitops_app_info_unique_app_without_svc_with_parent',
      'gitops_app_info_unique_app_without_svc_without_parent'
    );

  IF partial_count <> 4 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION
      'Aborting: expected 4 gitops_app_info_unique_app_* partial indexes, found %', partial_count;
  END IF;

  DROP INDEX IF EXISTS public.gitops_app_info_unique_application_index;
  RAISE NOTICE 'Dropped gitops_app_info_unique_application_index';
END $$;

COMMIT;

-- Verification: expect only the four gitops_app_info_unique_app_* partial indexes.
SELECT indexname
FROM pg_indexes
WHERE schemaname = 'public' AND tablename = 'gitops_app_info'
  AND indexname LIKE 'gitops_app_info_unique%'
ORDER BY indexname;
```

